  "problem": {
    "id": "train-6555",
    "question": "James injured his ankle and decides to slowly start working back up to his previous running goals and then surpass them.  Before the injury, he was able to run 100 miles per week.  He wants to get up to 20% more than that total in 280 days and each week he will increase miles walked in the week by the same amount.  How many miles does he need to add per week?",
    "gold": "3",
    "answer": "He wants to run 100*.2=<<100*.2=20>>20 miles more than he used to\nSo he needs to run 100+20=<<100+20=120>>120 miles\nHe is doing this in 280/7=<<280/7=40>>40 weeks\nSo he needs to add 120/40=<<120/40=3>>3 miles per week\n#### 3"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many miles James needs to add per week, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the target weekly mileage:**\n   James wants to run 20% more than his previous weekly mileage of 100 miles.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Target weekly mileage} = 100 \\text{ miles} + 0.20 \\times 100 \\text{ miles} = 100 \\text{ miles} + 20 \\text{ miles} = 120 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the total number of weeks:**\n   James has 280 days to reach his target. Since there are 7 days in a week, we convert the total days to weeks:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total weeks} = \\frac{280 \\text{ days}}{7 \\text{ days/week}} = 40 \\text{ weeks}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the total miles needed to be run over 40 weeks:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total miles} = 120 \\text{ miles/week} \\times 40 \\text{ weeks} = 4800 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the weekly increase in miles:**\n   James needs to increase his weekly mileage by the same amount each week. Let \\( x \\) be the number of miles he needs to add per week. Over 40 weeks, the total increase in miles will be \\( 40x \\). The total miles run over 40 weeks will be the initial 100 miles plus the total increase:\n   \\[\n   100 \\text{ miles} + 40x = 4800 \\text{ miles}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Solve for \\( x \\):**\n   \\[\n   100 + 40x = 4800\n   \\]\n   Subtract 100 from both sides:\n   \\[\n   40x = 4700\n   \\]\n   Divide both sides by 40:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{4700}{40} = 117.5\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, James needs to add \\(\\boxed{117.5}\\) miles per week.",
